I didn't want to dive into the specific tactics. To me, the fact that
I get a high success rate at PR is enough. Anyway:

> Being so wimpy that you have to rely on your pet is a risk; your pet
> will die and you stay alone with XL:1 and lousy HPs in a difficult

Honestly, I almost never feel worried about my pet. Trapdoors are a
real PITA, but most times I have went down and found my pet. With the
right set of Elbereth's and moves, you can dive to DLVL4 without
hitting once. I only feel worried about my pet when i guess that it's
low on HP and starts fighting a mimic, or when I arrive at the Mines
and hear rumbling in the distance. The trick for keeping your pet
alive is not letting it go down the mines untill it's a housecat or
dog (so it can survive traps), and finding mimics before it and not
letting it enter shops if you think it can be defeated, waiting till
your pet uplevels.

(horses are a different story. it's exactly the reverse: not letting
it grow up to a warhorse before minetown, or you may lose it to a
shopkeeper)

