You see, if all you have is a hammer everything looks like a nail. Of
course I'm more resourceful, taking advantage of what I know, what I
have, and what I know I will find and confront... but only after I've
done the PR. Doing the "other" strategy (advancing a dungeon level
when my xp level is one higher) often leaves me in a spot where I know
that I must go back and I can't go down, with nothing in my inventory
to let me progress. That never happens when you've done the PR. You
only find wimpy, laughable foes. The worse thing I usually find in
